// The boreal forest's own (V2-10, the first expansion wave): the larches, firs, spruces, pines,
// birches and aspens of the taiga in the Old World and the New, and its floor — berries, heaths,
// feather moss, sphagnum and reindeer lichen. Climates are the species' ranges in the cold
// continental forest (Köppen Dfc/Dfd/Dwc/Dwd) as rounded from general dendrology and boreal
// ecology references; the coldest of the taiga (mean −10 to −15 °C) is the larches'.
